================================================================================
1. OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Memory Beep is a single-button memory/pattern recall game inspired by the 
classic "Simon Says" game. Since only one button is available (rather than 
the traditional 4-color-button setup), this game encodes the pattern using 
SHORT and LONG button presses instead of different buttons/colors.

The game displays a growing sequence of SHORT and LONG flashes on screen 
(visualized as differently-sized bars). After watching the full sequence, 
the player must reproduce it exactly by tapping (short press) or holding 
(long press) the button in the same order. Each successful round adds one 
more step to the sequence, increasing the memory challenge.

GAME GENRE     : Memory / Pattern Recall
CONTROL SCHEME : Single Button (Short Tap = 0, Long Hold = 1)
DIFFICULTY     : Progressive (sequence grows by 1 each round; level 
                 increases every 3 sequence steps)
DISPLAY        : 128x64 OLED (SH1106 driver, SPI interface)
MICROCONTROLLER: Arduino Nano

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO PLAY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Power on the device - Start Screen appears showing "MEMORY BEEP"
2. Press the button to begin the game
3. WATCH PHASE: The screen flashes a sequence of bars:
   - A WIDE bar labeled "LONG" = a long flash
   - A NARROW bar labeled "SHORT" = a short flash
   - Watch carefully - the sequence starts with just 1 step and grows 
     each round
4. YOUR TURN PHASE: Reproduce the sequence using the button:
   - Quick tap (release before threshold) = SHORT input
   - Hold the button down (past the threshold) = LONG input
   - While holding, a growing bar shows your hold duration in real-time, 
     with a marker line showing exactly where "short" becomes "long"
5. If you reproduce the ENTIRE sequence correctly, you advance to the 
   next round (sequence grows by 1, harder to remember)
6. If you make ANY mistake, the game ends immediately
7. Press the button again on the Game Over screen to return to the start 
   screen and play again

