GAME STATE MACHINE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum GameState { START_SCREEN, SHOWING_SEQUENCE, WAITING_INPUT, 
                 ROUND_SUCCESS, ROUND_FAIL, GAME_OVER_STATE }

    This game uses a proper C++ ENUM to manage 6 distinct states, unlike 
    Flappy Bird and Stop The Bar which used simple boolean flags 
    (gameStarted, gameOver). This is a more scalable pattern for games 
    with multiple sequential phases.

STATE          | DESCRIPTION
----------------|---------------------------------------------------------
START_SCREEN    | Title screen, waiting for player to begin
SHOWING_SEQUENCE| Displaying the pattern the player must memorize
WAITING_INPUT   | Player is inputting their answer via short/long presses
ROUND_SUCCESS   | Brief "SEQUENCE COMPLETE!" display before next round
ROUND_FAIL      | Brief "WRONG!" display showing the correct expected input
GAME_OVER_STATE | Final results screen, waiting for restart

VARIABLE     | TYPE      | DEFAULT     | DESCRIPTION
-------------|-----------|-------------|------------------------------------
state        | GameState | START_SCREEN| Tracks which of the 6 states the 
             |           |             | game is currently in

