9. TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

ISSUE: Short presses are sometimes registered as long, or vice versa
FIX: LONG_PRESS_THRESHOLD (400ms) may not match the player's natural 
     tapping speed. Test with your target users and adjust the threshold 
     value accordingly. Also verify no mechanical button bounce is 
     adding extra milliseconds to press duration readings.

ISSUE: Game seems to "skip" or misjudge the first input after watching 
       the sequence
FIX: Ensure buttonWasPressed is properly reset to false when transitioning 
     from SHOWING_SEQUENCE to WAITING_INPUT state - if the button happens 
     to be physically held down at the exact moment of transition, this 
     could cause an incorrect initial reading. Consider adding an 
     explicit reset of buttonWasPressed = false in the transition code 
     within handleShowingSequence() when switching to WAITING_INPUT.

ISSUE: Display flickers excessively during the watch phase
FIX: This is expected behavior since drawFlash() is called every loop 
     iteration during the "ON" phase (redrawing the same frame 
     repeatedly). This is generally not visually problematic on OLED 
     displays, but if it becomes an issue, consider adding a check to 
     only call drawFlash() once when the phase begins, rather than 
     every loop iteration.

ISSUE: Sequence becomes impossible to remember at higher levels
FIX: This is a natural difficulty curve for memory games. If you want a 
     gentler curve, consider adding audio cues (if a buzzer is added to 
     your hardware) to reinforce visual memory, or slow down 
     SHORT_DURATION/LONG_DURATION at higher levels to give more 
     processing time per flash.

ISSUE: bestScore resets unexpectedly
FIX: Verify that bestScore is only updated within handleWaitingInput() 
     upon a MISMATCH (if (score > bestScore) bestScore = score;), and 
     that no other function accidentally resets this variable. Note 
     that unlike Stop The Bar's bestStreak, this variable is updated 
     ONLY on failure, not on every successful round - if you want it 
     updated continuously, you may need to add an additional check in 
     ROUND_SUCCESS handling as well.

